  "description": "Falernum can be tricky to find commercially, but it's easy to make at home so that you can be ready to mix up lots of classic cocktails.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 3 days 12 hr 35 min.\n\nNotes: I left the ginger out, because I think it takes over the flavor. However, many consider it a part of the traditional recipe. You can add a tablespoon of grated ginger with the lime zest, if desired.\nFalernum is best used within a month and does not need to be refrigerated.",
